    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d393">

                <pb facs="0582" n="462" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg462"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Tower to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-08-03"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 3, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 729.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose to you herewith
                    three copies of the Reichs-Gesetzblatt, No. 33, of the 15th of July, 1905,
                    containing the text in French and in German of a convention entered into by the
                    Imperial German Government on the 18th of May, 1904, at Paris, with the
                    Governments of Belgium, Denmark, Spain, France, Great Britain, Italy, the
                    Netherlands, Portugal, Russia, Sweden and Norway, and Switzerland for the
                    purpose of checking and controlling in the countries of the respective signatory
                    powers the traffic in girls (“traite des blanches,” “Mädchenhandel”).</p>
                <p>This convention was ratified by the contracting powers at Paris on the 18th of
                    January, 1905, and was published in Berlin on the 12th of July, 1905.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charlemagne
                    Tower.</hi></signed></closer>



